From: ROCKNIX/DUCKTALE
Subject: [PATCH] ufs-qcom: let VCC settle before the reference clock (SM8750)

A USB-C attach/detach while the SM8750 is in deep suspend wedges the SoC
hard (screen dead, 20s forced reset). The cable event wakes the AP right
while the PMIC is renegotiating its rails; UFS resume then powers VCC back
up and immediately starts the reference clock on a still-ramping supply.
Quiet suspends (no cable events) resume fine, and every resume already logs
ufshcd_set_timestamp_attr/Query RSP anomalies on linux 7.1.

7.1 introduced UFSHCD_QUIRK_VCC_ON_DELAY (a 1ms settle after VCC on in
ufshcd_vreg_set_hpm) for exactly this class of platform, but no host sets
it yet. Advertise it on qcom hosts.

--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1305,6 +1305,13 @@ static void ufs_qcom_advertise_quirks(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 	if (host->hw_ver.major > 0x3)
 		hba->quirks |= UFSHCD_QUIRK_REINIT_AFTER_MAX_GEAR_SWITCH;

+	/*
+	 * Give VCC time to settle before the reference clock starts: a resume
+	 * triggered by a USB-C attach/detach races the PMIC rail renegotiation
+	 * and an unstable VCC at refclk-on wedges the UFS device (SM8750).
+	 */
+	hba->quirks |= UFSHCD_QUIRK_VCC_ON_DELAY;
+
 	if (drvdata && drvdata->quirks)
 		hba->quirks |= drvdata->quirks;
 }
